+/*
+ * Experimental, versioned i915 checkpoint/restore interface.
+ *
+ * A session is transactional. Dump sessions freeze the drm_file state until
+ * COMMIT or ABORT. Restore sessions retain every newly created object until
+ * COMMIT and destroy them on ABORT. Version 2 supports idle ordinary shmem
+ * GEM objects shared between i915 file descriptions. Version 3 additionally
+ * preserves idle empty, signaled binary, and fully signaled timeline syncobjs.
+ * Version 4 preserves configured but not yet submitted contexts and empty
+ * explicit GPU VMs. Version 5 preserves idle materialized contexts using the
+ * default engine map and ordinary local object bindings at exact GPU virtual
+ * addresses. Version 6 accounts for retained i915-exported dma-buf descriptor
+ * references while refusing attachments and imported non-i915 objects.
+ * Version 7 preserves complete retained descriptor references for successful
+ * signaled binary sync_file exports whose source syncobj is unambiguous.
+ * Version 8 preserves primary/render node role, client capabilities, current
+ * DRM master ownership, single-plane linear framebuffers at exact IDs, and
+ * user-created KMS property blobs at exact IDs. Atomic property state remains
+ * a validated userspace image applied through generic DRM atomic ioctls.
+ * Version 9 adds exact per-VMA mmap-node provenance. Version 10 additionally
+ * preserves bounded user-selected physical engine maps. Version 11 preserves
+ * the implicit default-context VM and its exact local bindings. Version 12
+ * preserves idle, normal-view unbound VMA identities without creating a GPU
+ * page-table binding. Version 13 preserves one-plane X/Y-tiled local i915
+ * framebuffers while retaining their exact modifier and raw GEM contents. It
+ * still refuses userptr, protected content, virtual/balanced/parallel engines,
+ * per-engine
+ * SSEU overrides, active requests, special VMA views, leases, pending events,
+ * unsupported sync_file fence graphs, and unsupported KMS resources.
+ */
